-- title:
--   Finiteness and projectivity of R[[x,y]]/(φ₁,φ₂)
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative Noetherian ring and let $\varphi$ be a `Series R`, that is, a pair $(\varphi_0,\varphi_1)$ of formal power series in two variables over $R$, indexed by `Fin 2`, each $\varphi_i \in R[[x_0,x_1]]$. Assume that each $\varphi_i$ has vanishing constant coefficient, and that there is a natural number $N$ such that $X_i^N$ lies in the ideal generated by the range of $\varphi$, i.e. $x_0^N, x_1^N \in (\varphi_0,\varphi_1)$. The conclusion is a conjunction about the kernel algebra $\mathrm{KerAlgebra}\,\varphi$, which by definition is the quotient ring $R[[x_0,x_1]]/(\varphi_0,\varphi_1)$ (the quotient of `MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) R` by the span of the range of $\varphi$): it is a finite $R$-module, and it is a projective $R$-module. Nothing is asserted here about a formal group law or about an $\mathcal{O}_D$-action; only the pair of series and the two hypotheses on it enter.
--
--   This is the commutative-algebra content behind the notion of kernel of an isogeny of formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-modules: a quasi-finite relative complete intersection of relative dimension $0$ over a Noetherian base is finite locally free. It is used by the lemmas governing degrees of kernels, in particular the composition and divisibility statements for `HasKernelOfDegree`.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_FormalODModule_finite_and_projective_kerAlgebra_of_X_pow_mem.lean

